@startuml pipeline_run_compute_deployment
title ChatHealthy Pipelines - Run Compute Deployment\nSingle-VM (provider, backward compatible) and Two-VM (new pipelines)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 10
skinparam ranksep 16
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

legend top left
  Compute a run is given. The trigger tier and the data tier are shared;
  only the run's VM topology differs. Provider keeps the single-VM shape it
  has today; new pipelines (e.g. Medicare) run the two-VM shape.
end legend

rectangle "Trigger tier - Azure Automation Runbook\nauthenticates as pipelineEditor (Virtual Machine + Network Contributor)\nfires on schedule/webhook, writes the run manifest, exits in seconds" as RB #eef4fb

frame "A - Single-VM run   (provider - UNCHANGED, backward compatible)" as A #f3faf3 {
  node "Pipeline Run VM   Standard_D32s_v6   (ephemeral, per run)" as AVM #eaf3ea {
    component "Controller\ncontrol_runner" as ACTL #dbe9f7
    component "Worker\nspawned locally as a subprocess, per partition" as AWK #dbe9f7
  }
}

frame "B - Two-VM run   (new pipelines - e.g. Medicare)" as B #fff8ef {
  node "Controller VM   (small, ephemeral)\nidentity: pipelineController - front-end Mongo only\nholds the DevOps trust-anchor key - status API :6969 (mTLS)" as BCTL #eaf3ea {
    component "Controller\ncontrol_runner\nenqueues work_items; provisions Worker VMs at fan-out" as BCTLC #dbe9f7
  }
  node "Worker VM x N   (big compute, ephemeral, per run)" as BWK #eaf3ea {
    component "resident worker-agent\nstarted by cloud-init at boot\nclaims work_items, spawns the worker, heartbeats" as BWKA #dbe9f7
  }
}

rectangle "Data tier" as DAT #ffffff {
  database "Front-end cluster (always-on)\nfrontend.pipelineAdmin - coordination + work_items" as FE #fdf3d8
  database "Pipeline cluster (resumed for the run)\nstaging + built collections" as PC #fdf3d8
}

RB --> AVM : ARM PUT: create the run VM (provider)
RB --> BCTL : ARM PUT: create the Controller VM (new pipelines)
BCTLC --> BWK : ARM PUT: create Worker VM(s) at each fan-out step
BCTLC --> FE : enqueue one work_item per partition
BWKA --> FE : claim / heartbeat / complete
ACTL --> FE : run manifest / work_items
ACTL --> PC : staging + built data
BWKA --> PC : staging + built data
BCTLC --> PC : resume + scale

note bottom of B
  Coordination is the Mongo work_items collection ONLY - no controller->worker channel.
  The worker VM self-deletes on clean exit; the watchdog reaps what is left behind.

  Cardinality per step (PROPOSAL - confirm or correct):
    - source fetch / freshness / archival : one worker per source
    - NPI file / per-provider build + enrich : one worker per state - 52, or the
      states passed as run args - the same fan-out the provider pipeline uses
    - specialty rollup, indication-map build, conformance : single worker

  pipelineController holds the Azure rights it needs to create Worker VMs and
  creates them directly - the rights follow the work. Its Mongo access stays
  confined to the front-end cluster's pipelineAdmin; the compute-plane grant is
  separate.
end note

@enduml
